rcu: tiny RCU runs its callbacks without waking ksoftirqd

Tiny RCU (the RCU of a kernel without SMP) notes a quiescent state in
every context switch and, when callbacks wait, raises RCU_SOFTIRQ. A
softirq raised in task context wakes ksoftirqd, so a context switch made
two more. A pod start frees much with RCU (files, maple tree nodes, 9p
request ids, processes): during the nginx start ksoftirqd ran ~475 times,
about two thirds of all context switches.

The softirq is now only marked as pending. It runs at the next interrupt
exit or local_bh_enable(), at the latest at the next tick (10 ms), and the
idle loop runs it before the CPU sleeps, so no callback waits for long and
NO_HZ does not report pending softirq work.

Measured with tools/pod-bench (jkroepke/v86), the first pod of a fresh
process, 12 alternating runs: nginx 46.8M -> 45.3M guest instructions,
CPU time of the main thread -3.4 %.

diff --git a/kernel/rcu/tiny.c b/kernel/rcu/tiny.c
index dccccd6be..e94a01a43 100644
--- a/kernel/rcu/tiny.c
+++ b/kernel/rcu/tiny.c
@@ -56,7 +56,15 @@ void rcu_qs(void)
 	local_irq_save(flags);
 	if (rcu_ctrlblk.donetail != rcu_ctrlblk.curtail) {
 		rcu_ctrlblk.donetail = rcu_ctrlblk.curtail;
-		raise_softirq_irqoff(RCU_SOFTIRQ);
+		/*
+		 * Only mark the softirq as pending: the context switch
+		 * that calls this would otherwise wake ksoftirqd, which
+		 * costs two more context switches. The callbacks run at
+		 * the next interrupt exit or local_bh_enable(), at the
+		 * latest at the next tick, or in do_idle() when the CPU
+		 * has nothing else to do.
+		 */
+		__raise_softirq_irqoff(RCU_SOFTIRQ);
 	}
 	WRITE_ONCE(rcu_ctrlblk.gp_seq, rcu_ctrlblk.gp_seq + 2);
 	local_irq_restore(flags);
diff --git a/kernel/sched/idle.c b/kernel/sched/idle.c
index eb73b65ce..95b23df63 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/idle.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/idle.c
@@ -293,6 +293,13 @@ static void do_idle(void)
 	 */
 	nohz_run_idle_balance(cpu);
 
+	/*
+	 * Tiny RCU marks its softirq as pending in a context switch
+	 * without waking ksoftirqd. Run it before the CPU sleeps.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_TINY_RCU) && local_softirq_pending())
+		do_softirq();
+
 	/*
 	 * If the arch has a polling bit, we maintain an invariant:
 	 *
